# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTHZ - LIST LIMIT QUERY-PARAMETER EDGES: CUSTOMER LISTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# limit=0, -1, 501, 100000 are clamped with Math.Clamp (Pagination/ListQueryLimits.Normalize, 1..500,
# default 500; CustomerEndpoints.Lookup NormalizeCustomerLookupLimit, 1..25, default 10, for
# GET /api/customers/by-name only) and answer 200. A non-numeric limit=abc fails ASP.NET Core model
# binding for the nullable int parameter and answers 400. Neither path may ever answer 500.
# Any mechanic session reaches every endpoint here (this file signs in with the admin account). GET /api/admin/mechanics uses the same
# Normalize call but is AdminOnly, so it 403s before the clamp runs and is excluded.
# Full 5-value matrix, one per distinct clamp rule; the shared-clamp consumers live in list-limit-edges-nested.http.

# Signs in with the admin account: the admin is a mechanic person too (person_type mechanic), so it
# passes MechanicOnly, and nothing in this file depends on the Admin role.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@SessionEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@SessionPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup][Authz] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Authz] Login with the admin account (200 expected)
# @name csrfSource1
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{SessionEmail}}", "password": "{{SessionPassword}}" }

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('autoservice_csrf='))?.match(/^autoservice_csrf=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###


# ── Customers: GET /api/customers, full matrix (ListQueryLimits, Customers/CustomerEndpoints.Queries.cs) ──


### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers?limit=0 (200 expected, clamped to 1 row)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?limit=0

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 1

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers?limit=-1 (200 expected, clamped to 1 row)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?limit=-1

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 1

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers?limit=501 (200 expected, clamped to 500 rows)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?limit=501

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 500

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers?limit=100000 (200 expected, clamped to 500 rows)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?limit=100000

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 500

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers?limit=abc (400 expected, a non-numeric limit fails model binding - never 500)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?limit=abc

?? status == 400

###

# ── Customers: GET /api/customers/by-name, full matrix (own clamp, CustomerEndpoints.Lookup.cs) ──


### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=0 (200 expected, clamped to 1 row)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=0

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 1

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=-1 (200 expected, clamped to 1 row)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=-1

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 1

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=501 (200 expected, clamped to 25 rows)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=501

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 25

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=100000 (200 expected, clamped to 25 rows)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=100000

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.length <= 25

###

### [Case][Authz] GET /api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=abc (400 expected, a non-numeric limit fails model binding - never 500)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/by-name?name=Test&limit=abc

?? status == 400

###
